# Git commits — no Cursor attribution

When creating git commits:

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or any Cursor/agent attribution trailer.
- Do not use `git commit --trailer` for Cursor-related lines.
- Use plain commit messages only (`git commit -m "..."` or `-F file`).
- If the user asks to commit, prefer they run `git commit` themselves when possible.

This repo installs `.githooks/prepare-commit-msg` to strip Cursor attribution if the environment injects it anyway. Run `scripts/install-git-hooks.ps1` after clone.

Also disable **Cursor Settings → Agent → Attribution → Commit Attribution** in the IDE.
